# --- Secrets ---
.env

# --- Machine-local runtime state ---
# Everything the pipeline writes at runtime lives under data/ (see
# src/channel_vetting/core/paths.py). None of it belongs in a PUBLIC repo:
#
#   - Ledgers (quota_log, credit_log, gemini_log) are per-machine counters.
#     Committing them merges two machines' spend into one nonsense total, and
#     the credit ledger is real money.
#   - Caches (search_cache, external_handles_cache, transcript_cache,
#     video_topics_cache, metadata_screen_cache) are regenerable.
#   - gemini_cache, backtest_results and outreach_preview/ hold CREATOR PII —
#     names, model-written reasoning about named people, and in a
#     --send-configured tree real email addresses.
#
# Ignored WHOLESALE rather than file by file: a state file added later is then
# ignored by default, instead of being one forgotten commit away from being
# published. Only the .gitkeep is tracked, so a fresh clone has the directory.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# --- Python ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Local-only docs ---
# Plans, runbooks, audits and TODOs are working notes for whoever is running
# this, not part of the published project. README.md is the only tracked .md.
docs/

# --- Agent tooling ---
# .agents/ holds VENDORED third-party skills. skills-lock.json is tracked and
# records the source and content hash of each, so they are re-fetchable — the
# same split as a lockfile without node_modules.
.agents/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.superpowers/
.gstack/

# --- Node ---
# Pure-Python project with no package.json. Keep npm artefacts out in case a
# stray install ever drops them here.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
